# Keep README.md in sync with the codebase

`README.md` is the canonical entry point for this repository. It documents the
public API of `<aktion-app>`, the bundled component library, themes,
docs site pages, live examples, project layout, and the build / test workflow.

## Before any code change

1. **Read `README.md` first.** It tells you which features exist, which
   attributes / methods / events are public, and how the docs site and live
   examples are organised. Use it to orient yourself before touching code.
2. Skim the relevant section (e.g. *Built-in components*, *Themes*, *Routing*,
   *Project layout*) so your change stays consistent with the documented
   contract.

## After (or while making) a code change

If your change affects anything documented in `README.md`, update the README
in the same commit. Common triggers:

| If you change…                                              | Update in README.md                                |
|-------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| `src/element.ts` attributes / properties / methods / events | *Public API* tables (Attributes / Properties / Methods / Events). |
| `src/library/components/*` — add / remove / rename a component | *Built-in components* table and any inline example. |
| `src/theme/index.ts` — add / remove a built-in theme        | *Themes* table and the intro bullet count.         |
| `src/runtime/builtins.ts` — add / remove a `@Builtin`       | The "20+ built-in functions" bullet at the top.    |
| `src/prompt/generator.ts` — change emitted prompt sections  | The prompt-related bullets and the *Build* section if outputs change. |
| `scripts/emit-prompt.mjs` — change dist output filenames    | *Build the library and system prompt* code block.  |
| `docs/*.html` — add a new docs page or live example         | *Documentation site* table and / or *Live examples* table. |
| `package.json` scripts / dist outputs / Node engine reqs    | *Run it locally* section.                          |
| `tests/*` — add a new top-level test file                   | *Run the test suite* bullet list.                  |
| `src/` folder layout                                        | *Project layout* tree.                             |

If you are unsure whether a change is README-worthy, ask: would a new
contributor reading only `README.md` get a wrong or stale picture of the
project after this change? If yes, update the README.

## Don't

- Don't let `README.md` drift behind the code. If you ship a feature without
  documenting it here, the next contributor (and the LLM consumers reading
  this repo) will not know it exists.
- Don't duplicate `skills/aktion/` content into the README. Link to it instead —
  they have different audiences (human integrators vs. AI agents authoring full
  apps). See `.cursor/rules/aktion-skill-sync.mdc` for that skill's own rules.
- Don't invent CDN URLs, theme names, or component names in the README —
  cross-check against `src/library/index.ts`, `src/theme/index.ts`, and
  `docs/live-demos.html` first.
